{"name":"Island Embrace","hex":"#ded9b4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"island","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A contiguous area of land, smaller than a continent, totally surrounded by water.","A contiguous area of land, smaller than a continent, partially surrounded by water; a peninsula; a half-island."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To surround with water; make into an island.","To set, dot (as if) with islands."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/island"},{"term":"embrace","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To clasp (someone or each other) in the arms with affection; to take in the arms; to hug.","To seize (something) eagerly or with alacrity; to accept or take up with cordiality; to welcome."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of putting arms around someone and bringing the person close to the chest; a hug.","An enclosure partially or fully surrounding someone or something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/embrace"}],"entries":[{"title":"Embrace (English band Embrace album)","blocks":[{"text":"Embrace is the eponymously titled sixth studio album by English alternative rock band Embrace. The album, produced by vocalist Richard McNamara, was released on 25 April 2014 in Friday-release countries and on 28 April 2014 in the United Kingdom by independent record label Cooking Vinyl. The album was the band's first in eight years, after the release of their fifth studio album This New Day in 2006."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/cf/Embrace_-_Embrace.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embrace_(English_band_Embrace_album)","wikidata":"Q16991755"},{"title":"Island","blocks":[{"text":"An island or isle is a piece of land, distinct from a continent, completely surrounded by water. There are continental islands, which were formed by being split from a continent by plate tectonics, and oceanic islands, which have never been part of a continent. Oceanic islands can be formed from volcanic activity, grow into atolls from coral reefs, and form from sediment along shorelines, creating barrier islands. River islands can also form from sediment and debris in rivers. Artificial islands are those made by humans, including small rocky outcroppings built out of lagoons and large-scale land reclamation projects used for development."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg/330px-Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Island","wikidata":"Q23442"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Richard_McNamara%2C_guitarist_of_Embrace.jpg/500px-Richard_McNamara%2C_guitarist_of_Embrace.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Richard_McNamara%2C_guitarist_of_Embrace.jpg/1280px-Richard_McNamara%2C_guitarist_of_Embrace.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Richard_McNamara%2C_guitarist_of_Embrace.jpg/500px-Richard_McNamara%2C_guitarist_of_Embrace.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Guitarist and producer Richard McNamara contributed greatly to the recording and production of Embrace, serving as one of only two personnel working on the album outside the band itself.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARichard_McNamara%2C_guitarist_of_Embrace.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Gal%C3%A1pagos_penguin_%28Spheniscus_mendiculus%29_male.jpg/500px-Gal%C3%A1pagos_penguin_%28Spheniscus_mendiculus%29_male.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Gal%C3%A1pagos_penguin_%28Spheniscus_mendiculus%29_male.jpg/1280px-Gal%C3%A1pagos_penguin_%28Spheniscus_mendiculus%29_male.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Gal%C3%A1pagos_penguin_%28Spheniscus_mendiculus%29_male.jpg/500px-Gal%C3%A1pagos_penguin_%28Spheniscus_mendiculus%29_male.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Galapagos penguin is endemic to the Galápagos Islands.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGal%C3%A1pagos_penguin_(Spheniscus_mendiculus)_male.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Pteropus_seychellensis.jpg/500px-Pteropus_seychellensis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Pteropus_seychellensis.jpg/500px-Pteropus_seychellensis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Seychelles fruit bat has a major role in distributing the seeds of trees between islands, a form of oceanic dispersal.[24]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APteropus_seychellensis.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Finchadaptiveradiation.png/500px-Finchadaptiveradiation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Finchadaptiveradiation.png/500px-Finchadaptiveradiation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Adaptive radiation of finch A (Geospiza magnirostris) into three other species of finches on the Galapagos Islands. Due to the absence of other birds, Darwin's finches adapted to new niches. Their seed-eating beaks evolved to handle foods such as nuts, fruits, and insects.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFinchadaptive